==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Cooldown Equality}}

==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[Kory]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*6 [[General GreGory|General GreGories]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 60~63.33 seconds<sup>1,800f~1,900f</sup>.
*1 [[Deathkory]] spawns as the boss after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Berserkory]] spawns after 140 seconds<sup>4,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage uses Kory variants to do extreme Wave damage, General GreGories as dangerous pushers, and infinitely spawning Sir Seals that act as sources of money.

Unlike most of the other stages here, unless you are using a [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Blocker]], [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] are not recommended here, as they can easily be sniped by the Kories' Waves, rendering them a waste of a slot.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
Tankers, ranged [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave Immune]] units, and ranged Wave Shields are your friends here.
*[[Can Can Cat]]: While not immune to Waves, Can Can Cat 3 shots the Sir Seals at level 30, and 2 shots the Sir Seals at level 50. With the Extra Money [[Talents|Talent]], this will give you a huge income boost that can help you summon your more expensive units. While not very practical, if your Can Can Cat has the Target [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] Talent, you can potentially slow General GreGory down, giving your units some much needed breathing room. Needs some more investment in 2♛, but is still great there.
*[[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Cutter Cat]]: At level 30, Neo Cutter Cat can kill a Sir Seal in one hit while strengthened. Due to its Wave Immunity, it can also do some great damage to Berserkory. Be mindful that it does cost an [[Catfruit|Epic Catfruit Seed]] to evolve though. In 2♛, he must be at least level 36 to instantly kill the Sir Seals.
*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]]: Probably the most easily accessible Wave Blocker. Its cooldown is relatively unchanged here, so it can still be used to the same effect. Make sure to protect it however, especially from the General GreGories.
*[[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]]: Can hold the frontline well due to the Kories having relatively low base damage. Be sure to have a Wave Blocker behind it, as it will be a stepping stone for Waves. Also make sure to protect it from the General GreGories.
*[[Gloomy Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Costumed Witchy Neneko]]: If you have this unit, she can make this stage a lot easier, as she can block the Waves from far away. Her cooldown is also heavily reduced here, making her a lot more spammable.

Recommended Ubers:

*[[Greater Balrog Cat|Balrog Cat]]
*[[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Baby Cat]]
*[[Baby Garu (Uber Rare Cat)|UBERFEST Garu]]
*[[Dark Beastlord Garu|EPICFEST Garu]]
*Any similar tanky units with good damage
*Any ranged units [[Immune to Waves|immune to waves]]

